# Authenticated Windows Vista SP2 x86 kernel/HAL export baselines, for the
# import gate's hlprx86 profile: xhcihlpr.sys, the x86 helper (design record
# 18 section 15.11), which loads on Windows 2000 SP4, XP SP3, Vista SP2 and 7
# SP1 x86 and is gated against every kernel and HAL of all four
# (win2k-baselines.expected, winxp-x86-baselines.expected and
# hlprx86-win7-baselines.expected are the other sets). Until task 38.3 this
# was nt6x86-vista-baselines.expected, the nt6x86 profile of xhcimsi.sys,
# the NT 6 x86 MSI helper (section 8.2).
#
# Source: tools\vista-x86-extracted, the files the Phase 22 readings were
# taken from (legal-provenance.md section 4), measured 2026-10-10.
#
# **One kernel image, not every one an in-scope target can run.** Vista x86
# loads ntoskrnl.exe or, with PAE (the default with NX), ntkrnlpa.exe; both
# are built from one source and export the same names, but only ntoskrnl.exe
# is staged here. Extracting ntkrnlpa.exe and adding its row is owed (design
# record 18 sections 8.2 and 15.11); until then this manifest's claim is the
# uniprocessor non-PAE image's export table, stated as exactly that. The
# import descriptor names NTOSKRNL.EXE whichever image the loader binds it
# to.
#
# Format, identical to win2k-baselines.expected:
#   PACKED OUTPUT PROVIDER VERSION LENGTH SHA256
# The files were copied as they are; PACKED repeats OUTPUT.

ntoskrnl.exe ntoskrnl.exe ntoskrnl.exe 6.0.6002.18005 3549672 45C9CB0604B9DA7BA15E8824FF4B446064AB40FFA8412679A49EC16EAF36F7FC
